        "original_id": "f857db29-35ee-552b-b679-2b34a2865caf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Disporum, Boltonia, Disporum viridescens\n- Places: Asia, North America, eastern Asia, northern India, Japan, Indonesia, Russian Far East\n- Concepts: genera, species, flowering plants, sunflower family\n- Geography: 72nd meridian east, Greenwich, North Pole, South Pole, Arctic Ocean, Indian Ocean, Southern Ocean, Antarctica\n\nFacts:\n- Disporum is a genus of about 20 species of perennial flowering plants commonly known as fairy bells.\n- Disporum is found in Asia from northern India to Japan, south to Indonesia, and north into the Russian Far East.\n- Boltonia is a genus of plants in the sunflower family that is native primarily to North America and has one species in eastern Asia.\n- Disporum viridescens is a species of flowering plant in the genus Disporum.\n- The 72nd meridian east of Greenwich is a line of longitude that runs from the North Pole across the Arctic Ocean, Asia, the Indian Ocean, the Southern Ocean, and Antarctica to the South Pole.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
